    "result": "Perfect! All 5 new threshold tests pass. The only failures are pre-existing issues. Let me create a summary of the changes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval` as requested. Here's what was implemented:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**1. frai-core (SDK layer)**\n- **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`**: Updated `generateReport()` to accept an optional `thresholds` parameter that maps metric IDs to minimum scores. Returns `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array with results.\n- **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`**: Updated markdown reporter to include a \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold.\n- **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`**: Added 5 new tests covering all threshold scenarios.\n\n**2. frai-cli (Command line)**\n- **`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`**: \n  - Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (can be given multiple times)\n  - Added `parseThresholds()` function with validation\n  - Validates metric IDs against available metrics\n  - Sets exit code to 1 when any threshold fails, 0 when all pass\n  - Exit code 2 for usage errors (malformed thresholds, unknown metrics, out-of-range values)\n  - Includes helpful error messages with valid metric IDs\n\n**3. Documentation**\n- Updated both `packages/frai-core/README.md` and `packages/frai-cli/README.md` to document the new `--threshold` option\n\n### Features Implemented\n\n\u2705 `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option for `frai eval`  \n\u2705 Multiple thresholds supported (e.g., `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.8`)  \n\u2705 Thresholds are optional (backward compatible)  \n\u2705 Score comparison: threshold passes when `metric.score >= min`  \n\u2705 Metrics with no score fail their threshold  \n\u2705 JSON reports include `passed` field and `thresholds` array  \n\u2705 Markdown reports include \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL statuses  \n\u2705 Exit codes: 0 if all pass, 1 if any fails, 2 for usage errors  \n\u2705 Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations()`  \n\u2705 Proper error messages with valid metric IDs listed for unknown metrics  \n\n### Test Results\n\nRunning eval tests: **7 passed, 1 pre-existing failure**\n- All 5 new threshold tests pass \u2713\n- Works with custom metrics \u2713\n- JSON and Markdown reports both include threshold info \u2713",
